From 179ff511fcd222fb5738d187770c5bdb83d03dae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Philippe Gerum <philippe.gerum@exail.com>
Date: Fri, 15 Mar 2024 15:38:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 0177/1013] igb: add oob I/O capabilities

Enable the IGB driver for out-of-band I/O traffic. In a nutshell, this
entails the following steps:

- turn on/off oob delivery for the NIC interrupts upon request from
  the in-band stack.

- use an oob-accessible page pool for RX.

- make sure TX only synchronizes the CPU caches instead of streaming
  DMA buffers when receiving data living in an oob-accessible page
  pool.

Signed-off-by: Philippe Gerum <philippe.gerum@exail.com>
---
